---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Private Anecdata" description="Structured, identifier-free reports of what people experience when they take peptides, published as honest counts.">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>What do people experience when they take peptides?</h1>
    <p class="lede">Most peptides have little or no human data. This site helps fill that gap by collecting peptide users' <a href="#why-anecdata">anecdata</a>. We encourage honest reporting through our <a href="#privacy-first">privacy-first methodology</a> and <a href="#public-interest">public interest commitment</a>.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/contribute">Contribute a report</a>
      <a class="alt" href="/data">See what is published</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how" id="how-this-works">
    <h2>How this works</h2>
    <p>You submit your experience without telling us who you are. We aggregate submissions and report them honestly.</p>
  </section>

  <details class="sec">
    <summary><h2>Why anecdata?</h2><span class="kicker">Anecdata can't replace randomized controlled trials. But anecdata &gt; no data.</span></summary>
    <div class="sec-body"><span id="why-anecdata" class="anchor"></span>
      <p>Anecdotal data (or "anecdata") cannot replace randomized controlled trials. Everything collected and published by this site is self-reported and unverified. Anecdotal evidence is never sufficient to substantiate claims about a health product. Nothing here is evidence that any compound is effective or safe. Nothing here is a recommendation.</p>
      <p>But anecdata is better than no data. Millions of people are already using peptides with limited understanding of the potential benefits and risks. Regulators are scrambling to make critical decisions with little to go on.</p>
      <p>Honest, structured anecdata is better than the anecdotal reports currently available on the internet. Peptide users have real experience, but their reports are scattered across unstructured forum posts and for-profit websites with questionable privacy practices.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="sec">
    <summary><h2>Privacy-first methodology</h2><span class="kicker">Strong privacy encourages more reporting.</span></summary>
    <div class="sec-body"><span id="privacy-first" class="anchor"></span>
      <p>We don't want to know who you are and will never ask. No name, no email, no IP address logging. We publish only aggregate statistics and will never publish, sell, or voluntarily share individual reports.</p>
      <p>Because no report is linked to a person, we cannot find and delete your report after you submit it. Submission is final. If that is not acceptable to you, please do not submit.</p>
      <p>Read our <a href="/docs/privacy-protocol">privacy protocol</a> before you submit.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="sec">
    <summary><h2>Public interest commitment and honest reporting</h2><span class="kicker">Rejecting profit helps ensure accurate reporting.</span></summary>
    <div class="sec-body"><span id="public-interest" class="anchor"></span>
      <p>Nobody pays us for this, and that will never change. No ads, no affiliate links, no sponsors, no selling or licensing of data, no paid tier.</p>
      <p>Other websites and apps that collect peptide anecdata are typically funded by advertisers, affiliates, sponsors, and/or data brokers. This raises questions about the accuracy of their reporting. We cannot say whether any for-profit site reports dishonestly. We can say that we have avoided the question altogether.</p>
      <p>Every accepted report is committed to a public append-only log. Anyone can confirm that the number we display is the number of reports that exist. Learn more about <a href="/docs/release-spec#how-we-count">how we count reports</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</Base>
